 "scenes": [
  {
   "turn": 1,
   "narration": "You sit nervously at your desk, clutching your weak copper training wand, as Professor Vance clears his throat to begin the practical assessment. Dust motes dance in the golden light cutting through the tall windows of Classroom 3-B, drifting lazily over chalkboards covered in dense runic formulas. Your oversized academy cloak feels suffocatingly warm, and your heart drums a frantic beat against your ribs.\n\nFrom the front row, Elara Vane tosses her head, her piercing blue eyes flicking back to look at you with cold amusement. She lightly taps her sleek mahogany wand against her palm, a spark of perfect blue spark dancing off its tip without a single drop of sweat. She knows, as everyone does, that you are the bottom of the class—the girl whose hands shake too much to light a simple candle.\n\n\"Silence,\" Professor Vance's voice cuts through the whispers, sharp and dry as old parchment. He adjusts his spectacles and unrolls a heavy scroll. \"Today we test the basic ignition rune. One by one, you will step up and light the brazier. Miss Sterling, since you require the most practice, you shall begin.\"\n\nAll eyes turn to you.",
   "player_action": null
  }
 ],
